seville.content:
Read 4 pages on Visita Sevilla. For a first visit, base yourself in Santa Cruz or the adjacent Arenal: they put the historic core within easy walking reach. Santa Cruz is atmospheric, with narrow streets, white houses, orange-tree plazas, and sights including the Alcázar, Cathedral and Giralda, Archivo de Indias, and Jardines de Murillo. Its official tourism page notes it is especially busy, so choose a quieter nearby street if you want a calmer stay.

Day 1 — Historic heart: Explore Santa Cruz’s lanes and plazas, then visit the Real Alcázar and Cathedral/Giralda. Allow time for a relaxed dinner nearby.

Day 2 — Old-town west and river: Visit Plaza de Toros/El Arenal and Torre del Oro, then cross to Triana for its market, ceramic heritage, and riverside walk. Check attraction opening times and book timed-entry tickets before you go.

Day 3 — Grand plazas and parks: Spend the morning at Plaza de España and Parque de María Luisa; add Plaza de América if energy allows. Return through the center for a final wander or visit the Museo de Bellas Artes.

Map: https://visitasevilla.es/mapa-interactivo-sevilla/ — the official interactive map includes Santa Cruz, El Arenal, Triana, Plaza de España, the Alcázar, Cathedral/Giralda, and many other landmarks.

