framework.content:
Read 12 pages on Framework, Phoronix, PCWorld, and Tom’s Hardware. Some available independent coverage is hands-on or for an earlier generation rather than a current-generation review.

{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en","title":"Framework | Framework Computer | Modular Laptops & PCs You Can Repair","facts":["The site identifies Laptop 13 Pro, Laptop 12, and Laptop 16 among its laptops.","Laptop 13 Pro is described with Intel Core Ultra Series 3 processors and a 20-hour battery-life claim.","Laptop 12 is described with Intel Core Series 3 processors; Laptop 16 with AMD Ryzen AI 300 Series processors."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/laptop13pro","title":"Framework | Framework Laptop 13 Pro: Intel Core Ultra 3 & LPCAMM2","facts":["Framework’s Laptop 13 Pro specifications list 1.4 kg weight, Intel Core Ultra Series 3 processors, and battery estimates of 20 hours of Netflix streaming, 17 hours of active web use, and 11 hours of video conferencing, under the stated test settings.","Framework names reviews from Phoronix, PCWorld, Tom’s Hardware, Gizmodo, and others on the product page."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/laptop12","title":"Framework | Order your Framework Laptop 12 now","facts":["Laptop 12 is a 12.2-inch convertible with Intel Core Series 3 processors; the page states up to 4.8 GHz and 2 performance plus 4 low-power efficiency cores.","The page lists 1.3 kg weight and says Core Series 3 delivers up to 70% longer Netflix 4K streaming battery life than the previous generation; it does not state a total runtime."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/laptop16","title":"Framework | Order a Framework Laptop 16 with AMD Ryzen™ AI 300 Series","facts":["Laptop 16 configurations list AMD Ryzen AI 5 340, AI 7 350, and AI 9 HX 370 processors, with respective prices starting at €1,409, €1,754, and €2,094 in the observed DIY configurator.","The product page lists weights of 2.1 kg with the Expansion Bay Shell and 2.4 kg with the Graphics Module, and an 85 Wh battery; it does not state runtime."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/products/laptop13pro-diy-intel-ultra-3/configuration/new","title":"Framework | Configure Framework Laptop 13 Pro DIY Edition (Intel®","facts":["The DIY configuration lists Intel Ultra 5 325 at €1,349, Ultra X7 358H at €1,909, and Ultra X9 388H at €2,139; each configuration lists a 74 Wh battery."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/products/laptop12-diy-intel-series3/configuration/new","title":"Framework | Configure Framework Laptop 12 DIY Edition (Intel® Core™","facts":["The Laptop 12 DIY Series 3 configuration starts at €619; listed processor options are Core 3 304 (€619), Core 5 320 (€879), and Core 7 350 (€1,129)."]}
{"url":"https://frame.work/at/en/products/laptop16-diy-amd-ai300/configuration/new","title":"Framework | Configure Framework Laptop 16 DIY Edition (AMD Ryzen™ AI","facts":["The Laptop 16 DIY AI 300 Series configuration lists starting prices of €1,409 for Ryzen AI 5 340, €1,754 for Ryzen AI 7 350, and €2,094 for Ryzen AI 9 HX 370."]}
{"url":"https://www.phoronix.com/review/framework-laptop-13-pro","title":"Framework Laptop 13 Pro: Aiming To Be One Of The Best Upgradeable Linux Laptops Review - Phoronix","facts":["Phoronix’s review identifies the Laptop 13 Pro as using Intel Core Ultra Series 3 and a 74 Wh battery, and reports weight of 1.4 kg.","The reviewer says Framework claimed up to 20 hours of battery life but does not publish its own battery benchmark result."]}
{"url":"https://www.pcworld.com/article/3199054/framework-laptop-13-pro-review.html","title":"Framework Laptop 13 Pro review: Easy to build, frustrating to buy | PCWorld","facts":["PCWorld’s July 2026 review lists Intel Core Ultra 5 325 as tested, 74 Wh battery, 3.13 pounds weight, and a tested price of $1,823; its price table showed $1,833 at Framework.","The review describes strong battery life but notes lengthy shipping and fluctuating prices."]}
{"url":"https://www.tomshardware.com/laptops/framework-laptop-13-pro-review","title":"Framework Laptop 13 Pro review: It cleans up nice | Tom's Hardware","facts":["Tom’s Hardware’s July 2026 review says the Laptop 13 Pro starts at $1,199 without SSD, RAM, or operating system, $1,599 prebuilt, and was approximately $3,272 as tested.","The review describes long battery life and an expensive product, but the visible page did not include specific runtime or weight figures."]}
{"url":"https://www.tomshardware.com/laptops/framework-laptop-12-review-wildcat-lake","title":"Framework Laptop 12 (Wildcat Lake) review: Growing up amid an unprecedented shortage | Tom's Hardware","facts":["Tom’s Hardware’s October 2026 review covers the Laptop 12 with Intel Wildcat Lake and describes it as repairable and portable, but comparatively costly unless buyers supply RAM and SSD.","The review page’s visible excerpt did not state battery runtime or weight."]}
{"url":"https://www.phoronix.com/review/framework-laptop-16-2026","title":"Framework Laptop 16 With GeForce RTX 5070 12GB, One-Piece Keyboard & Haptic Touchpad - Phoronix","facts":["Phoronix’s 2026 review describes the Laptop 16 with an optional GeForce RTX 5070 12 GB graphics module, new haptic touchpad and one-piece keyboard, and reports good Linux support.","The visible introduction does not give price, weight, or battery runtime."]}
{"url":"https://www.tomshardware.com/laptops/framework-laptop-16-review","title":"Framework Laptop 16 review: the Franken-notebook | Tom's Hardware","facts":["Tom’s Hardware’s January 2024 review calls the 2024 Laptop 16 customizable with upgradeable graphics and reports $1,749 as tested; this is earlier-generation coverage, not a review of the latest configuration."]}
{"url":"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2215545/framework-laptop-16-review.html","title":"Framework Laptop 16 review: The perfect laptop for PC hardware nerds | PCWorld","facts":["PCWorld’s February 2024 review lists the earlier Laptop 16 with Ryzen 9 7940HS, 85 Wh battery, 5.29 pounds, and a starting price of $1,399; its review configuration was approximately $2,400.","The reviewer describes good battery life for a laptop with discrete graphics. This review is for the 2024 model, not the latest AI 300 Series configuration."]}
{"url":"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2423486/framework-laptop-13-review.html","title":"Framework Laptop 13 review: Build your own laptop | PCWorld","facts":["PCWorld’s 2024 review covers an earlier Framework Laptop 13, listing Intel Core Ultra 7 155H, a 61 Wh battery, 2.87 pounds, and a €1,249 reviewed price; it is not a review of the current 13 Pro."]}
{"url":"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2618070/framework-12-reinvents-budget-laptops-with-new-amd-cpus.html","title":"Framework 12 aims at 'janky, locked-down, disposable, underpowered, and frankly boring [laptops]' | PCWorld","facts":["PCWorld’s February 2025 preview describes Laptop 12 as a 2-in-1 convertible with a 13th-generation Intel Core option, up to 48 GB RAM, and up to 2 TB storage; it did not report a product price or measured runtime.","This is an early preview, not an independent review of the current Series 3 model."]}
